  "description": "Event Name: Techashy 2.0 – 24-Hour National-Level Hackathon Organized By: Beta Labs, the premier technical club of IIIT Kottayam Flagship event under Aaroh 2026 – the annual tech-fest Event Overview: Techashy is a 24-hour national-level hackathon bringing together student developers, engineers, and innovators from across India. Participants ideate, design, and build functional solutions to real-world problem statements within an intense 24-hour development cycle. The event emphasizes practical implementation, scalable architecture, and deployable prototypes. Event Specifications: Duration: 24 Hours Mode: On-site Venue: IIIT Kottayam Campus Team Size: 3–5 Members Problem Domains: Healthcare & MedTech AI & Machine Learning Agriculture & Climate Tech Smart Cities & IoT Education & EdTech Blockchain & Cybersecurity Social Good & Governance What Participants Will Build: End-to-end functional prototypes Scalable and demo-ready solutions Full-stack or domain-focused systems addressing industry-relevant challenges Architects reviewed under live mentorship from technical experts and professionals Why Participate: National-level competitive exposure Direct interaction with industry mentors and recruiters Networking with top technical talent across the country Potential fast-track recruitment and pre-placement opportunities Hands-on experience building under real-world constraints and tight deadlines Learning Outcomes: Strengthens technical problem-solving ability Enhances teamwork and collaboration Develops rapid prototyping and execution skills Encourages innovation-driven and production-ready thinking Techashy is designed to push boundaries and cultivate the next generation of engineers capable of building impactful, real-world solutions under pressure.",
